	;(defconst secondary-build 8)
	;(defconst resource-needed 5)
	;(defconst rush-control 6)
	;(defconst resource-supp 9)
	;(defconst combat-arm  11) 
	; Z: These two are the relics of the original unit training system, whereby each civ was assigned a major unit type and a secondary unit type to train
	;  While the idea was sound - allowing for different unit comps each match - the execution was incredibly lacking
	;  Major blunders like Empire sidelining Mech, Wooks never going HW, etc, alongside nonsensical unit constants meant it never did its intended job
	;  When I was rewriting the unit train logic, I made them call the constants no matter what this rolled, which functionally depreciated the file, although the file, combat-arm, does remain intact (just never loaded)
	;(defconst attack-enabled 13)
	;(defconst age-advancement 14)
	; Z: ah, the legendary upgrade-conflict, responsible for so much stupid and incomprehensible code
	;  and actively made the AI worse by NOT picking up techs because "it didn't have enough units for them to affect" (because they were being spawncamped)
	;  the original script that contained this goal is an exercise in "less is more" - if it was just as simple as (can research tech) => (research tech) the AI would have been 300% less stupid
	;  (but still very stupid, because combat-arm prevented it from picking up stuff like mech range)
	;(defconst upgrade-conflict 16)
	;(defconst personality 18)
	;(defconst castle-attempt 21) ; Uses: NO, YES, ANOTHER ; Z: another big stupid goal that was so much easier (and better!) to write as "can build fortress -> build fortress"
	; Z: Sometimes the GB devs didn't even name their goals and only left notes in the constant file. Super user-friendly and easy to understand! Thanks! /s
		;goal 22 = used to help in diplomacy
		;goal 24 = used to control the CP stopping giving away tribute to the player when asked to do so
		;goal 25 = controls alliance & resource types
		;goal 29 = controls tribute for feeder personalities 
		;goal 35 = used for diplomacy on Easy & Easiest difficulty levels only. Also used to track used to calculate enemy navy size on higher levels of difficulty
		;goal 36, 37, 38, 39 = carbon, food, nova, metal checks for script parts that require them.
	;(defconst sea-owner 23) ; Uses: NO, YES, NOTICE
